## v0.7.6 – Login Page Redesign with Display Cards and Request Invite Flow

**Date:** December 25, 2024

### Changes Made:
- Redesigned login page with two-panel layout (grey25 left panel, white right panel)
- Added ASTROTASK logomark and tagline to left panel: "A Privacy Focused Kanban built for Makers And Creatives"
- Styled "KANBAN" as uppercase, font-weight 900, grey975 color
- Positioned branding 140px from left, 180px from top
- Added "Get an Invite" button below login button with 40px gap
- Made login button disabled until both email and password are entered
- Added display-only NewTaskCard component (non-interactive, 548px width)
- Added display-only expanded Card component (non-interactive, 480px width)
- Set display card content: "Task Title", "Design"/"Kanban" tags, "Astrotask" project
- Made display card labels grey300, tags right-aligned (scoped to display only)
- Added ephemeral timer: Session 1 static at 00:12:20, Session 2 counts up from 00:00:00
- Main timer displays Session 2 only, Total shows Session 1 + Session 2
- Made chevron button always visible and clickable for expand/collapse toggle
- Added auto-collapse after 3 seconds when card loads in expanded state
- Added fadeSlideUp animation (140px, 1s, cubic-bezier) for display cards
- Staggered animations: NewTaskCard immediate, expanded Card delays 0.5s
- Removed play/pause icon from display card
- Created new /request-invite page with email and message form
- Added /request-invite to PUBLIC_ROUTES in RouteGuard
- Backend: Added SendInviteRequestNotification function to email.go
- Backend: Added RequestInvite handler to auth.go with email package import
- Backend: Added public route POST /api/v1/auth/request-invite
- Frontend: Connected request-invite form to backend API endpoint
- Updated success message: "We'll send an invite to [email] when we are ready for more users!"

### Current Status:
- Login page has full two-panel layout with animated display cards showcasing the product
- Display card timer counts up in real-time, auto-collapses after 3 seconds
- Request invite flow is fully functional: form submission sends email notification to admin
- Email sent via Resend API (or logged to console if RESEND_API_KEY not set)

### Unresolved Issues:
- None

